{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778522407,"nonce":"SoKQWccM8JIXkX9PIAdFlYwYFDg=","title":"Commit channel-server dist on main following 4e32923 merge","message":"Issue `4e32923` merged to main (commit `906d5ff`) without committing the `channel-server` build output. Per Mandible CLAUDE.md (\"Do not commit `dist/` in feature branches. Build once in the integration branch after all feature merges, then commit the dist there\"), the feature branch was correct to omit `dist/`; the **integration-time** build was the step that was missed before the auth request.\n\nTo allow dotfiles wiring (`497fafa`) to register `mcpServers.mandible` pointing at `dist/channel-server/index.js`, the built output needs to land on `main`.\n\n## Mechanical follow-up\n\n1. `npm run build:channel-server` from a fresh feature branch off `main`.\n2. Commit the resulting `dist/channel-server/` files.\n3. Auth-request to `main`.\n\nAfter merge, the dotfiles change can land (or merge first if it lands without verification — channel server fails-soft if the path doesn't exist, so ordering is preferred but not strict).\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Auto-rebuild post-merge / post-pull (tracked in a sibling issue).\n- Any source changes to `channel-server/`.\n\n## Cross-refs\n\n- `4e32923` (the merged work)\n- `497fafa` (dotfiles wiring that depends on this)","files":null}]}